// A genuinely-missed edge ticks at wake (design/wake_catchup.md): in1
// fired while the sampling arm slept, unread by the selected arm —
// held — so the wake delivers it FIRED and `~` ticks (9). This is the
// case that killed uniform-stale-at-wake: an edge consumer must catch
// up on exactly the fires no selected reader saw.
// Expected trace (both engines): 0; <quiet>; 9.
// schedule-v1: cap=208 events=1664; in1=i64:5; in0=i64:1
{let v0 = select in0 {i64:0 => i64:0, i64:1 => in1 ~ i64:9, _ => i64:-1}; v0}
